## Unicode.org — `8859-1.TXT`

`src/testdata/8859-1.TXT` is vendored verbatim from
https://www.unicode.org/Public/MAPPINGS/ISO8859/8859-1.TXT (table version 2.0,
dated 1999-07-27, header last updated 2015-12-02): the normative ISO/IEC
8859-1:1998 -> Unicode mapping. WHATWG does not publish a separate index table
for this page — in the WHATWG algorithm the *label* "iso-8859-1" is an alias
for the windows-1252 *encoding*, but this module's `iso_8859_1` is the true,
distinct ISO/IEC 8859-1 code page (pure Latin-1 identity high half), so
Unicode.org is the correct normative source here instead. Driven by the same
`normative_vectors.zig` / `normative_test.zig` pair (a second parser, since the
column layout differs from the WHATWG files).

The file's own header:

    # 8859-1.TXT
    # © 2015 Unicode®, Inc.
    # For terms of use, see http://www.unicode.org/terms_of_use.html

Under the Unicode License v3 (https://www.unicode.org/license.txt):

    Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a
    copy of data files and any associated documentation (the "Data Files") ...
    to deal in the Data Files ... without restriction ... provided that
    either (a) this copyright and permission notice appear with all copies
    of the Data Files ... or (b) this copyright and permission notice appear
    in associated Documentation.

Only conformance DATA is reproduced from either source — no WHATWG or
Unicode.org source code is present in this module. The implementation under
test (`decodeToUtf8`/`encodeFromUtf8`/the per-page tables in `root.zig`) is
the authors' own (MIT), modeled after the WHATWG Encoding Standard's
single-byte European subset as design reference (recorded in the root
`NOTICE` §2), not copied from it.
